  <section><para>Here is a graph of \(y= f(x)\) where \(f(x) = 3x+2\).</para>
<image alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION WITH A \(y\)-intercepts OF 1 AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS 1 COMMA 2, 2 COMMA 4, AND 3 COMMA 8." class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="295" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/dbe8e515126db8d5055c1d1ac574a4b5688f3dbd" width="300"/><para>How do the values of \(f\) change whenever \(x\) increases by 2?</para></section>
